WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.650
<i>Haru, a young apprentice period 
who's cheerful and nice to everyone.</i>

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:07.150
<i>But...</i>

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.820
What's going on here, Iona-san?

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.860
I keep rolling and only getting 
one-stars! This is impossible!

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.880
<i>Haru, exhausted, raises his
 voice against a lady.</i>

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.580
<i>What happened to this good, 
hardworking young man?</i>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.380
<i>And what will be his fate?</i>

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.560
This is what we warned you about.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.950
<b>~ the journey to the end of the despair ~</b>

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.600
<i>Docky-Docky Documentary</i>!

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:04.810
"The Bottomless Swamp of No Return!"

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:07.770
<b>Episode 5: The Swamp's Name</b>

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:13.160
Okay, it's that time again! 
For <i>Docky-Docky Documentary</i>!

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.820
I'm your host, the Mayor!

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.640
And I'm his assistant, Ashiko.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:22.580
First, let's introduce our guests.

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:26.810
You know them from the Animal Realm's
 super-popular program <i>Working Bear</i>.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:30.340
They're White Bear and Black Bear, 
the Monochrome Bears!

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.540
Hi there!

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:37.780
And from the Sky Realm, the prophet
 who documents all, Oracle-san!

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.130
Thanks for having me.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.910
But that period... Haru-kun, was it?

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.270
What happened to him?

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:45.560
He looked like such a good kid.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.340
He was broken by capitalist exploitation.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.390
It happens to grown-ups a lot.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.950
He was definitely a kid, though.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.640
First, let's take a look.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.360
No matter what his fate is,

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.930
it's already been decided.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.530
The hard-working
 apprentice period, Haru-kun...

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:03.430
Our team met him when

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.970
he'd been hired to exterminate 
spirals from a certain village.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.880
Everybody, it's time for the documentary!

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.160
Docky-docky!

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:24.080
Okay!

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:27.800
Hey there! Good work, docu!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.960
You let us document some quality period work!

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.720
Sorry we surprised you by asking
 permission to shoot our documentary.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.980
Nah, it's fine.

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.840
Did I look good on camera?

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:44.210
If I knew we were filming, I would've 
worn an outfit like I did last week!

00:03:44.210 --> 00:03:47.470
You documented perfectly!

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:51.450
Wow, nobody's even bothering to 
point out that it's the same guy.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:55.090
Um, by the way...

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.200
Why are you filming us?

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.050
So we can make a documentary, of course.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:04.430
Our village has made its living 
off of documentaries for years.

00:04:05.250 --> 00:04:09.720
Quality documentaries can find 
buyers from all of the six powers!

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:11.230
I see!

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.470
Wow!

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.200
After documenting the way
 you fought, I'm sure of it!

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:19.650
Our next documentary is going 
to be about young periods!

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:23.610
So, can we follow you around 
and document you up close?

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.880
F-Follow us around?

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.770
Get nice and close!

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.160
Choco!

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.200
Sure!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.800
Anything you want! We're fine with it!

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.500
At last, the whole world will 
learn about our heroics!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.320
I need to make an appointment 
to get my nails done!

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:39.040
Can I get one soon?

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.010
A TV show, huh?

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.720
<i>Hopeless, the old capital of the Huma Realm.</i>

00:04:44.570 --> 00:04:46.880
<i>This town, famous for its hope buns,</i>

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.010
<i>is where their HQ,
 Branch Office #8, is located.</i>

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:55.130
Watch your step.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.420
Sorry.

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:00.050
This is my room.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:03.360
I used to share a room with Gajeru and Liza,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.780
but it was too small.

00:05:06.380 --> 00:05:08.100
<i>The roof seems to be missing.</i>

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.430
Yeah, that's why it's cheap.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:13.920
<i>We were told that Branch Office #8
 is in financial trouble,</i>

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:16.120
<i>but Haru seems to be doing just fine.</i>

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:20.840
<i>He says he recently got a bonus, 
which he put into his savings.</i>

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:24.170
I'm satisfied with the way I live now.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.730
Sure, being a period isn't easy, but...

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:31.720
It's satisfying.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.120
My plan is to just not 
make any big purchases,

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:36.840
except maybe a treat for 
Choco every once in a while.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:38.190
That's the kind of life I want to lead.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.790
Haru, I don't need any big treats.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.590
Just feed me steak and chocolate every day.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:46.610
Yeah, that's asking for a lot.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.560
Haru-san is always very good to me.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:54.020
He gave me a home, a job...

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:54.850
Yeah.

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:56.910
The people at the office are nice, too.

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.310
We don't get to do much during combat,

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:01.060
but we want to repay him someday.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.500
Well, the best a one-star 
character can expect to.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:07.370
<i>One day, Haru used a vacation day</i>

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.470
<i>to show us a local cafeteria,
 Nia's Restaurant, where he's a regular.</i>

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.400
I see.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.560
You and your friends are
going to be in a documentary?

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:17.000
That's right.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.510
So these guys are following
us around doing in-depth interviews.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:21.640
Nice and close!

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.460
That's enough of that...

00:06:24.040 --> 00:06:25.520
I'm hungry.

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:27.550
Feed me something, anything.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.860
I get it.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:31.830
Kokotto-san, I'll take 
two of the daily lunches.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:34.160
Yes, with pleasure!

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:35.950
Welcome!

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.120
Hey, Kokotto!

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.600
Gilled-san!

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.130
Brother Gilled?

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.920
Hey, is that you, Haru?

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:45.760
Don't "is that you" me!

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:47.820
Where have you been, brother?

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:50.440
Branch Office #8 is in big trouble,

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.760
but we haven't seen you at all!

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.710
Noin, you say something, too.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.950
Brother, it's been so long.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.240
Yeah, it sure has.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.600
Wait, now's not the time for greetings!

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:06.770
<i>These two are Gilled, an older period,
 and Noin, who works for HQ.</i>

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:10.480
<i>By chance, they reunited today 
for the first time in months.</i>

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:11.610
I'm sorry, Haru.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.080
I was upset about Branch Office #8,

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:18.500
but I was so busy with a mission 
for HQ that I couldn't stop by.

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.590
Sorry, Big Brother!

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:22.900
I-I see...

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.090
<i>Also, none of them are actually related.</i>

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.170
But I heard the rumors.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:32.090
You new kids are working really hard.

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:33.930
Yeah.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:38.390
Friendship between men is 
enough to give me a nosebleed,

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:42.800
but I'm so mad he's interfering 
with my reunion with Gilled.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.810
Let it go. He's Haru.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:47.440
I'll at least draw a doujin, I guess.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.570
Now, Haru-kun's life may seem pretty good.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.960
What do you think, White Bear?

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:58.720
Yeah, he looks so happy!

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.950
He's got money, a fulfilling job,

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:04.250
a cute girlfriend, and the 
older periods love him!

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:06.320
What else could he want?

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:07.550
That's right.

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:10.210
I'm curious how this is a swamp.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.600
What do you document, Oracle-san?

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:17.560
I've sealed away my prophetic powers for 
today so I can enjoy the program,

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:20.770
but I still have a bad feeling.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.330
I think the next person Haru-kun 
meets will determine his fate.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.500
Perhaps that's just my intuition 
after years as a prophet?

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.510
Maybe you're just too worried?

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.690
Hey, you'll make her mad!

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.950
I hope it is just me.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:36.940
Everything's coming up roses for Haru-kun.

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:39.920
But on his way back from the cafeteria,

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.540
he encounters an unexpected person...

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:46.580
Will Oracle-san's guess be proven right?

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.990
Let's find out!

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.340
Docky-docky!

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.050
I'm so glad I got to see those two again.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:55.130
I feel full of energy now.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.800
Yeah. It might be a set-up, though.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.490
<i>It definitely wasn't.
 We didn't send them there.</i>

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:01.010
<i>It was pure chance.</i>

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:03.540
We have to tell Erika-san, too!

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:06.940
Maybe she'll get mad and tell 
them to stop by the office?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.070
I-Iona-san?

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.300
Iona-san, are you okay?

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.530
What happened?

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.990
H-Haru-kun...

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.080
<i>A surprising twist,
 right after these messages!</i>

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.080
<b>~ the journey to the end of the despair ~</b>

00:09:28.180 --> 00:09:30.040
You really saved me.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.440
I haven't eaten anything lately.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:34.980
Really, thanks.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:37.480
I'm glad you're not sick,

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:39.360
just hungry.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:43.230
Lately, the economy's so bad 
that nobody's making any calls.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:48.170
You remember how those two zellionaires 
were spending money like it was water,

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.200
and then they vanished all of a sudden?

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:55.200
It blew up the economy and 
made a mess for everybody.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.140
I... I see.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.620
Those jerks.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.330
Oh, right.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.410
This is the amount I 
borrowed from you before.

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:06.670
It's late, but...

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.090
Oh, that's fine.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.160
I'm just glad you're paying me back.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:14.420
Hang on, I'll get your change.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.960
It's fine.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.330
You can have it all as an 
apology for me being late.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:20.380
I can't do that.

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:21.890
Here you go.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:24.430
What's this?

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.000
They're pretty but weird rocks.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.320
These are luna stones.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:31.750
They provide the energy you use to make calls.

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:33.730
Twenty-five gives you one call.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:38.910
They're very valuable, so normally 
you pay for them in yen, not zel.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:41.720
I didn't know that!

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:44.860
During emergencies, I'll sell them for zel,

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.790
but I take a big commission.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.770
At this rate...

00:10:49.770 --> 00:10:54.280
You get forty, plus the 
set bonus is twenty, so...

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:57.780
So then I take back what 
I lent you for one call,

00:10:57.780 --> 00:11:00.910
and you get thirty-five stones back!

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:05.320
Can I make another call with this?

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:06.680
That's right.

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.640
If you've got the money to spare,

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.140
do a bunch more calls, okay?

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:14.890
If you buy a lot of luna stones 
at once, you get more as a bonus.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.730
Anyway, thanks for the meal.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:20.400
I think you'll get a powerful 
character with your next call.

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.120
Yeah, I hope so!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:24.520
See you around!

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:26.660
Bye-bye!

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:30.660
If Wiseman gets in our way again,

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.880
maybe I'll make another call.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.090
I'm doing it to help people, after all.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.750
Buy, buy, buy!

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:41.890
Thank you very much!

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:45.720
<i>Where did you go?</i>

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:47.560
After my conversation with Iona-san,

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.050
I decided to buy some luna stones.

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:50.670
<i>You bought a lot, huh?</i>

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:53.010
The more you buy, the more you save.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.380
So I bought a lot.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.060
<i>Did you talk to the rest 
of the office about it?</i>

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.000
No, I didn't.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:00.530
It's up to me whether I call or not.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:04.240
But I know it'll make a 
difference in our missions!

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:07.100
<i>Any reluctance to rely on calling?</i>

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:11.870
I think it would best if we were strong 
enough to do everything ourselves,

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:13.800
but we're not there yet.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.870
I think calling and putting 
together a good party

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:20.170
is another way for periods to fight.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.910
If I can do that and then 
gradually get stronger,

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:24.760
that will be good, I think.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.260
<i>And you'll pay any amount of zel to do that?</i>

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:29.450
Don't worry.

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:32.980
Erika-san, my boss, says the same thing.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:34.810
If you don't do it in moderation,

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:36.230
you'll get stuck in a swamp!

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.400
Oracle-san was right!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.060
After meeting the girl named Iona,

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:46.990
he was documented buying massive
 amounts of luna stones.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:50.100
But he's still in control of himself.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:53.880
His boss's words are still fresh in his mind.

00:12:53.880 --> 00:12:57.050
He's a good kid. I think he'll be fine.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.870
Right?

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:01.920
Hmm, I can't see this ending 
without something happening.

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:07.560
After meeting Iona-san that day, 
Haru-kun bought extra luna stones.

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.640
His fate is about to take a big turn!

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.670
This is where the documentary gets good!

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:14.440
Let's get back to it!

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:15.730
Docky-docky!

00:13:16.460 --> 00:13:19.610
<i>That morning, Branch Office #8
 was in an uproar.</i>

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:22.680
<i>They'd gotten three quests at once,</i>

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:28.620
<i>and Gajeru, Liza, and Haru were 
all heading off on missions alone.</i>

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:33.240
First, as we discussed,
 head for the quest locations.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:34.480
If we're doing three at once,

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:37.220
that means at least two of 
them will be Wiseman-free.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:41.290
We'll have to wait and 
see who gets interrupted.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.450
I think it'll be Haru!

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:45.900
He's friends with them lately.

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:47.730
Me, too!

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:48.640
Me three!

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.560
We're not friends!

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:52.810
So it'll be Haru, then.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.600
No, we don't know that yet.

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:58.920
Wiseman.

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.280
Yeah, I knew it was going to be me.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.160
That's your cue!

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:05.820
Luluna!

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.200
Right.

00:14:07.800 --> 00:14:10.120
Time to call!

00:14:15.910 --> 00:14:18.150
Where am I?

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:21.250
It's not... the poison swamp.

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:24.920
Welcome, guru!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:25.630
Did you see that?

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:29.050
The Poison Witch from the 
Blood Realm, Zaku-san!

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.080
Zaku-san? Non! Zaku-tan!

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:33.900
Call me that.

00:14:33.900 --> 00:14:36.390
R-Right... sorry, guru.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:39.750
I can call, too!

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.180
Iona-san!

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.190
Coming!

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:45.650
You asked for Iona-chan, and here she is!

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:47.930
Thanks, Haru-kun!

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:50.280
You've decided to call, huh?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.160
Yes.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.120
Just like you said, I got some luna stones.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.620
Wow, you bought a bunch at once, huh?

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.960
That's great!

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.420
Yeah, I'm doing it to help people!

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:04.440
Huh? Haruharu, how many 
calls are you going to make?

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:08.380
If he makes that many calls,
 he'll definitely get a strong character!

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.510
Yeah, yeah!

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:15.530
Okay, let's start with ten calls, Iona-san!

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:18.140
Okay, time to call!

00:15:58.260 --> 00:16:00.020
Let's let loose with a big one!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:03.790
One! One! One!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.490
Hey, what the hell is that?

00:16:07.490 --> 00:16:08.940
I can't believe it!

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:11.520
Ten rolls that only give you one-stars?

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:14.340
Wh-What's going on here, Iona-san?

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:16.640
It's all one-stars again!

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:18.410
That's weird.

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:20.010
But it's all random chance.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.500
So sometimes it happens.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.880
But I'm using luna stones!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.100
Those aren't even supposed to give one-stars!

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:29.830
Ten rolls is supposed to
 guarantee a four-star!

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.340
Well, this is real life.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.800
It doesn't work here like it does in a game.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:43.700
Fine.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:45.690
I'll do single rolls this time.

00:16:46.410 --> 00:16:48.270
I'm not letting it end like this.

00:16:48.270 --> 00:16:51.300
Okay! Here we go!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.130
Hang on a second!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:11.890
I'm draining the account dry!

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.880
Cancel my fixed-term deposits, too!

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:22.770
I'd like to buy luna stones
 with zel directly.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:26.900
Sure, but like I said,
the commission is hefty...

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:27.850
I don't care!

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:38.740
What is going on here, Iona-san?

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:43.120
I keep rolling and only getting 
one-stars! This is impossible!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:47.250
But who you get on a roll 
is a matter of probability.

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.960
And the probabilities are messed up!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:53.710
Come on, if I draw this many,
 aren't you supposed to help me out?

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.520
There's gotta be some way to help me!

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:57.320
This is definitely a bug!

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:01.140
Are you listening, Iona-san?

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:04.580
Am I supposed to just take this 
horde of one-stars home with me?

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.230
I can't do that!

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:08.680
If I quit now, I'll have nothing left.

00:18:08.680 --> 00:18:11.450
I'm definitely going to get something
 on my next roll, right? Right?

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:14.170
Guarantee it, Iona-san!

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:16.250
I can't make guarantees,

00:18:16.250 --> 00:18:18.840
but some day, the probabilities 
should turn in your favor.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:19.660
Right?

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.010
Right?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:22.740
I can't stop here, can I?

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:27.210
Give me more luna stones!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:30.240
H-Hey, you should stop, right?

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:31.270
That's right!

00:18:31.270 --> 00:18:34.420
When things aren't going your way,
 it's always smart to stop for a while!

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:36.020
Yeah! Yeah!

00:18:36.020 --> 00:18:38.880
Next time, I might get something amazing!

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:41.570
This is between me and the calls!

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:43.850
This isn't any of your business, so butt out!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:46.040
It's not our business?

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:48.480
We're the ones you're fighting.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:50.700
Is he okay?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:53.020
Once you get like that, you can't go back.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:54.350
Yeah.

00:18:54.840 --> 00:18:59.360
A swamp's a swamp because you can't get out.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:13.000
This is the last of it.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:18.670
I put every zel I had into these calls.

00:19:19.190 --> 00:19:20.930
Please!

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:24.280
Give me a strong character!

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.560
Okay, here goes the call!

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:28.640
I can see it!

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.980
You can talk with me, but it won't be fun.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:39.890
Congratulations! I'm so happy for you.

00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:41.750
Bye-bye!

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:44.540
Haru?

00:19:45.040 --> 00:19:46.000
Haru?

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:48.790
Haru!

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.860
<i>"Serious call addiction."</i>

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:53.900
<i>That was the doctor's diagnosis.</i>

00:19:58.450 --> 00:20:02.000
Well, that was a horrible ending.

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.800
What did you document, everyone?

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.320
It truly is a swamp!

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:10.020
Even if your life's going just fine,

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:11.630
you can still get stuck in it.

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:13.520
Maybe it's easier to get stuck 
when things are fine.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:17.610
They say that everybody has a desire for 
self-destruction somewhere in their heart.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.150
So it can happen to anybody,

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:22.320
I bet.

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:27.040
But of course, calling itself
 isn't a bad thing!

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:31.160
Everybody, just remember to 
do all things in moderation!

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:32.990
Ding-dong!

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:35.400
Now, as for what happened to Haru-kun...

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.320
Fortunately his symptoms were light,

00:20:37.320 --> 00:20:40.530
and after a few days of rehab, 
he was back to being a period.

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:43.220
But he also paid an unexpected price!

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:47.100
Tonight, we'll sign off as we watch his fate.

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.760
See you next week on...

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:52.030
<i>Docky-Docky Documentary</i>!

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:58.340
All the people I called disappeared?

00:20:58.340 --> 00:21:00.120
We couldn't help it.

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:05.530
After you spent all your zel, we didn't 
have the money to keep them here.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:06.360
Aw...

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:10.240
Those first two monks 
worked really hard, too.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.710
But they said if everybody else 
was leaving, they couldn't stay.

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:17.640
We're leaving the roof today, too.

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:21.000
I guess we're back to
 four in a room again, huh?

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:24.340
Yeah, sorry, everyone.

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.430
I told you.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:31.880
It's a swamp.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:44.680
I wish I could've said thanks 
to Haru before we left.

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:49.370
Yeah. "Thanks for summoning us."

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:52.580
Will we see him again?

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:54.440
We sure will.

00:21:54.440 --> 00:21:57.040
Someday... I know it!

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Episode 6
Confessions of a Mask</b>

00:23:36.650 --> 00:23:38.810
"Confessions of a Mask."
